WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.540
I am standing in a line at Trader Joe's,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.370
and I cannot believe I'm standing in

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.530
a line at Trader Joe's because I hate.

00:00:07.845 --> 00:00:08.805
Trader Joe's.

00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:11.385
Trader Joe's is a bullshit grocery store.

00:00:11.385 --> 00:00:12.945
It is a store where I can go in and

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.865
get hot dogs and buns, but I can't

00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:16.814
get the Doritos and the Diet Coke or

00:00:16.814 --> 00:00:18.165
even the aluminum foil that I need to

00:00:18.165 --> 00:00:20.235
put on the grill to cook the hot dogs.

00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:22.125
This is, this is a grocery store

00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:23.805
that requires you to have another

00:00:23.805 --> 00:00:25.575
grocery store, and that is bullshit.

00:00:25.935 --> 00:00:27.735
You walk in and there's no aisles.

00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:29.055
People just mill around like

00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:31.935
sheep and look for things The.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.290
The, the registers are all equipped

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.090
with this bell because if register

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.740
three needs pennies, they ring the bell.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.750
'cause everyone in the goddamn store needs

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.610
to know that register three needs pennies.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.860
I hate everything about this store and

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.750
the only reason I'm here is 'cause my

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.670
daughter, Clara, loves the pizza bites

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.710
and Charlie loves the fish sticks and my

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.960
wife likes every goddamn thing in this

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.019
store, but I'm not even in the store.

00:00:55.019 --> 00:00:56.310
I'm outside the store.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.350
In a socially distanced line,

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.580
this gathering of people,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.290
because it is May of 2020.

00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:02.635
Early in the pandemic.

00:01:02.635 --> 00:01:03.955
And the only thing Trader Joe's

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:05.695
does well is they only let a few

00:01:05.695 --> 00:01:07.135
people into the store at a time.

00:01:07.135 --> 00:01:08.665
So at least it's safe.

00:01:08.905 --> 00:01:10.105
So I'm standing in this

00:01:10.105 --> 00:01:11.185
line for this store.

00:01:11.185 --> 00:01:13.795
I hate for people, I love, and I'm just

00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:16.345
trying to keep the peace and I cannot,

00:01:16.615 --> 00:01:18.655
'cause there is a woman, three people

00:01:18.655 --> 00:01:20.725
in front of me, and she's turned,

00:01:20.725 --> 00:01:22.705
she's turned to us and to her audience.

00:01:22.755 --> 00:01:25.244
She is masked and she's telling us how

00:01:25.244 --> 00:01:27.914
unfair it is that she's being masked.

00:01:27.914 --> 00:01:30.015
She cannot stand the fact that she's

00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:31.935
being forced to wear this awful thing.

00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:33.195
And there's all these

00:01:33.195 --> 00:01:34.725
things I wanna say to her.

00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:36.914
'cause the one superpower I have in

00:01:36.914 --> 00:01:39.195
this world is I know the worst thing to

00:01:39.195 --> 00:01:41.774
say to someone to make them feel bad.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.985
I am the person at CVS where if it's a

00:01:44.985 --> 00:01:46.725
long line and the woman turns and says,

00:01:46.725 --> 00:01:48.615
can you believe how slow this cashier is?

00:01:48.735 --> 00:01:50.235
I say in a very loud voice.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:51.710
Why are you telling me

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.030
how slow the cashier is?

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.140
She's right up there.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:55.669
You shouldn't talk behind her back.

00:01:55.669 --> 00:01:57.110
And my wife runs and the woman goes

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.169
crazy at the Patriots game when, when

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:02.929
the guy in row 17 says, Hey, take your

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:04.789
hat off during the national anthem to

00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:06.560
the poor guy in row five who forgot.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:07.639
I'm the guy who turns

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:08.930
around and says, yeah, ha.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:09.380
Police.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:10.459
That is a lot less

00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:11.660
disruptive than the hat.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.459
I'm so glad you shouted at the

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:15.410
man during the national anthem.

00:02:17.924 --> 00:02:19.364
But my wife has told me I'm going

00:02:19.364 --> 00:02:21.195
to get killed someday, and she's

00:02:21.195 --> 00:02:22.695
asked me to stop doing this.

00:02:22.695 --> 00:02:24.674
So I'm letting the lunatic scream

00:02:24.674 --> 00:02:26.505
about the mask and I look at my phone

00:02:27.015 --> 00:02:29.355
and then she says the word sacrifice.

00:02:29.595 --> 00:02:31.035
She says she's making a great

00:02:31.035 --> 00:02:33.524
sacrifice to have to go into the store

00:02:33.524 --> 00:02:35.144
and something just snaps with me.

00:02:35.505 --> 00:02:38.144
And I look up and I say, excuse me.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.049
My father was drafted and he

00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:41.640
had to fight in Vietnam, a

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.230
war he did not wanna fight in.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.030
He was exposed to Agent Orange.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.800
He's had four heart attacks and a

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.390
heart condition for all his life.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.429
So when I go home today, I'm

00:02:50.429 --> 00:02:52.109
gonna tell him about the fucking

00:02:52.109 --> 00:02:54.899
hero I saw in the line who made

00:02:54.899 --> 00:02:57.000
the sacrifice to wear the mask.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.209
And he's gonna be amazed and she loses her

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:04.109
mind and she starts screaming for the poor

00:03:04.109 --> 00:03:06.089
lady in the Trader Joe's line to like.

00:03:06.365 --> 00:03:07.625
Have me arrested.

00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:08.915
She wants to call the police.

00:03:09.005 --> 00:03:10.505
The guy behind me does not help.

00:03:10.505 --> 00:03:12.515
He says He didn't verbally abuse you.

00:03:12.515 --> 00:03:13.835
He called you a hero.

00:03:13.985 --> 00:03:15.005
And that doesn't help.

00:03:15.665 --> 00:03:17.315
It doesn't help in any way.

00:03:18.155 --> 00:03:19.415
And I realize I've created these

00:03:19.415 --> 00:03:21.095
situations that my wife warns me

00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:22.265
about, and I realize the only way

00:03:22.265 --> 00:03:23.765
to get out of it is I have to leave.

00:03:24.335 --> 00:03:25.745
So I tell the Trader Joe's employee,

00:03:25.745 --> 00:03:26.735
you don't need to call the police.

00:03:26.735 --> 00:03:27.245
I will leave.

00:03:27.245 --> 00:03:28.415
I'll come back later as I leave.

00:03:28.415 --> 00:03:29.675
She says, that's right.

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:30.185
Walk away.

00:03:30.185 --> 00:03:31.775
And it is everything in

00:03:31.775 --> 00:03:33.095
me to not turn around.

00:03:33.165 --> 00:03:35.385
Yeah, but I don't, I get in the car

00:03:35.385 --> 00:03:37.454
and I drive home, and as I'm driving,

00:03:37.454 --> 00:03:38.954
I'm thinking about my wife and how she

00:03:38.954 --> 00:03:40.454
says this is a bad thing to do, but I

00:03:40.454 --> 00:03:44.295
think it's not because there's crazy

00:03:44.295 --> 00:03:46.215
people in the world that say terrible

00:03:46.215 --> 00:03:49.155
things and good decent people just

00:03:49.155 --> 00:03:51.255
have to listen to it all the time.

00:03:51.704 --> 00:03:52.454
And I just think.

00:03:53.085 --> 00:03:55.485
Maybe I can be the crazy person that says

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:57.465
the right thing to the other crazy people.

00:03:57.765 --> 00:03:59.565
So maybe the next time she thinks

00:03:59.565 --> 00:04:00.855
about turning around, she'll think

00:04:00.855 --> 00:04:04.245
maybe I'm there, and maybe she'll stop.

00:04:05.415 --> 00:04:06.795
I'm a social justice

00:04:06.795 --> 00:04:08.235
warrior, that's what I think.

00:04:08.805 --> 00:04:10.545
I think that until I turn onto

00:04:10.545 --> 00:04:12.765
my street and I see our house and

00:04:12.765 --> 00:04:15.015
suddenly my body is filled with glee.

00:04:15.885 --> 00:04:17.474
I can't wait to tell my wife

00:04:17.474 --> 00:04:18.584
what I just did, even though

00:04:18.584 --> 00:04:19.755
I know she's gonna be mad.

00:04:19.755 --> 00:04:23.534
I am so excited about it and it's

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:27.104
that glee that makes me realize that

00:04:27.104 --> 00:04:29.205
I am not a social justice warrior.

00:04:30.284 --> 00:04:31.875
I just really love.

00:04:32.385 --> 00:04:35.895
To yell at people and make them feel

00:04:35.895 --> 00:04:38.745
bad when they deserve to feel bad.

00:04:39.975 --> 00:04:41.295
As I'm driving towards my house,

00:04:41.295 --> 00:04:43.395
I realize that if the entire world

00:04:43.395 --> 00:04:46.305
suddenly became universally kind

00:04:46.305 --> 00:04:49.155
and benevolent, I would be upset.

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:51.255
I would.

00:04:53.085 --> 00:04:54.735
As I pull into my driveway,

00:04:55.245 --> 00:04:57.525
I think I am really no better

00:04:57.525 --> 00:04:59.145
than that lunatic in the line.

00:04:59.145 --> 00:05:02.355
I. Because I am not shouting at her

00:05:02.955 --> 00:05:04.875
because I want the world to change.

00:05:05.595 --> 00:05:07.455
I'm shouting at her because I really

00:05:07.455 --> 00:05:09.765
like shouting at terrible people.

00:05:10.305 --> 00:05:11.895
And if they were to all go away.

00:05:13.395 --> 00:05:17.865
That would be a sad day for me, so my wife

00:05:17.865 --> 00:05:20.565
is wi, my wife is right as she always is.

00:05:20.865 --> 00:05:23.775
I need to shut my damn mouth and move

00:05:23.775 --> 00:05:25.995
on in my life and be a better person.

00:05:26.595 --> 00:05:26.955
Thank you.

